1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,180
Ollie: Good morning, Pip! It's a perfect day!

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:09,030
Gus: Look what Gran Mari gave me! A job!

3
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:11,550
Gus: I get to look after this seed!

4
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:15,880
Pip: It looks like a tiny rock.

5
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:19,590
Ollie: But it's not a rock. It's a seed!

6
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:27,480
Ollie: What does a seed need?

7
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:31,830
Ollie: Let's find out!

8
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:06,290
Pip: Where should the seed go?

9
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:10,870
Ollie: The dark shelf! It's closest. Quick, quick!

10
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:15,680
Pip: Ollie, you didn't ask anyone!

11
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:22,760
Ollie: Oops. I rushed again. What do you think, Bean?

12
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:28,830
Ollie: Great idea, Bean! It's warm and bright here.

13
00:01:30,330 --> 00:01:34,550
Gus: Job done! The seed is on the sill. Time to play!

14
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:38,610
Pip: Doesn't a seed need more than a sill?

15
00:01:40,110 --> 00:01:44,950
Gus: I've got a faster way! Seeds grow all by themselves.

16
00:01:46,450 --> 00:01:49,950
Gus: I'll check on it later. Much later!

17
00:01:50,350 --> 00:01:53,730
Pip: What if we try the careful way? Let's ask Gran Mari.

18
00:01:55,970 --> 00:02:00,140
Ollie: Okay. We'll check on the seed tomorrow.

19
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:14,560
Ollie: Today the seed grows! I bet it's huge!

20
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:20,310
Ollie: It didn't change at all!

21
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:26,030
Gus: Is it a tree yet? I did not forget!

22
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:28,310
Pip: Gus, did you give it anything to drink?

23
00:02:29,810 --> 00:02:34,770
Gus: Drink? Um. Yes! Lots. It drank it all. Very fast.

24
00:02:36,270 --> 00:02:40,810
Ollie: But the jar is dry, Gus.

25
00:02:41,210 --> 00:02:46,060
Gus: That's just its dry look! Very fashionable!

26
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:52,090
Gus: Seeds like it warm! I'll hatch it!

27
00:02:58,590 --> 00:03:02,090
Gus: Whoa! I'm fine! I meant to do that!

28
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:06,990
Ollie: Gus, what does a seed really need?

29
00:03:07,390 --> 00:03:11,920
Gus: I don't know. Seeds are small. How hard can it be?

30
00:03:18,110 --> 00:03:21,240
Ollie: We need help. Let's ask Gran Mari.

31
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:33,200
Gran Mari: Well now, a yarny seagull and a puzzled otter. What's all this?

32
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:38,870
Ollie: Gran Mari, what does a seed need?

33
00:03:40,370 --> 00:03:50,480
Gran Mari: Oh, that is a good question, Ollie. Let's find out together.

34
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:04,600
Gran Mari: I set these up last week. Same seeds, same sunny window.

35
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:11,840
Gran Mari: Only one thing is different. The towel.

36
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:15,140
Ollie: That looks just like our seed.

37
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:18,900
Pip: This one is waking up!

38
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:31,920
Gran Mari: Water wakes a seed up. A warm spot helps too. Then the green shoot reaches for the light.

39
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:35,260
Ollie: It's growing toward the sun!

40
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:44,640
Gran Mari: Well now, what do you think happens next?

41
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:52,320
Ollie: The seed wakes up! But not right away.

42
00:04:53,820 --> 00:05:01,450
Gran Mari: Right. A seed takes time. It can't be hurried.

43
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:14,900
Ollie: Try it at home! Ask a grown-up to help you.

44
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:19,620
Ollie: Wet a paper towel and fold it. Put it in a clear bag with a bean.

45
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:25,080
Ollie: Tape the bag to a sunny window. Check it every day.

46
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:30,110
Gus: I have to say something. I fibbed.

47
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:36,660
Gus: I said it drank lots. It didn't. I forgot all about it.

48
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,720
Ollie: Thanks for telling us, Gus.

49
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:57,420
Gus: One shell for every day I check. That's my job.

50
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,950
Bean: Water!

51
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:10,740
Gus: You're right, Bean! I almost forgot again!

52
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:27,220
Gus: It's growing! It's really growing!

53
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:34,230
Pip: Look! A tiny green hat on a seed!

54
00:06:43,730 --> 00:06:47,510
Ollie: Time for my Wonder Pocket! Three things we learned.

55
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:54,400
Ollie: One. A seed needs water to wake up.

56
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:59,610
Ollie: Two. A warm, sunny spot helps it grow.

57
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:06,870
Ollie: Three. A seed needs time. We can't hurry it.

58
00:07:08,370 --> 00:07:13,220
Ollie: And one kind thing to try today. Look after something small. Give it water!

59
00:07:15,550 --> 00:07:18,530
Gus: Bye, everybody! I'm off to water my seed!
